From 2ebaf2d45071d568d23e6570811bd63fb7cde633 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bruce Ashfield <bruce.ashfield@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:26:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] x86/Kconfig.cpu: pin CC_HAS_MARCH_NATIVE off for reproducible
 builds

CONFIG_CC_HAS_MARCH_NATIVE is a def_bool computed from
$(cc-option, -march=native), i.e. it is probed from the build-host
compiler. In cross builds the result varies by build host -- the kernel's
own comment already notes "This flag might not be available in
cross-compilers" -- so it is captured differently across otherwise
identical builds and breaks kernel package reproducibility:

  .config / auto.conf:  CONFIG_CC_HAS_MARCH_NATIVE=y   (host A) vs absent (host B)
  autoconf.h:           #define CONFIG_CC_HAS_MARCH_NATIVE 1
  .config:              # CONFIG_X86_NATIVE_CPU is not set
  rustc_cfg:            --cfg=CONFIG_CC_HAS_MARCH_NATIVE

With CONFIG_IKCONFIG=y the .config is gzip-embedded into the kernel
(kernel_config_data), so the difference also propagates into
vmlinux/bzImage/kernel-dbg (the blob shifts kernel_config_data_end and
every symbol after it), failing reproducibility across the whole kernel
package set -- not just the config text files, which is why a post-package
filter is not sufficient.

CC_HAS_MARCH_NATIVE gates only X86_NATIVE_CPU ("build and optimize for
local/native CPU"), which is never enabled in these builds and is
antithetical to a distributed/reproducible kernel. Pin the symbol off so
the captured config is deterministic regardless of build host. On-target
'make scripts prepare' uses this same patched Kconfig, so it recomputes
the same value and needs no reconfiguration.

Signed-off-by: Bruce Ashfield <bruce.ashfield@gmail.com>
---
 arch/x86/Kconfig.cpu | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/x86/Kconfig.cpu b/arch/x86/Kconfig.cpu
index e4654388d794b..1c8e709daf0ae 100644
--- a/arch/x86/Kconfig.cpu
+++ b/arch/x86/Kconfig.cpu
@@ -195,8 +195,14 @@ config MATOM
 endchoice
 
 config CC_HAS_MARCH_NATIVE
-	# This flag might not be available in cross-compilers:
-	def_bool $(cc-option, -march=native)
+	# yocto: pinned off for reproducible builds. The upstream
+	# 'def_bool $(cc-option, -march=native)' is probed from the build-host
+	# compiler and varies across cross build hosts, so it (and the
+	# X86_NATIVE_CPU line it gates) is captured differently in the kernel
+	# config -- and via CONFIG_IKCONFIG into the image -- breaking
+	# reproducibility. It only gates X86_NATIVE_CPU, which is never enabled
+	# here, so pinning it off has no functional effect.
+	def_bool n
 	# LLVM 18 has an easily triggered internal compiler error in core
 	# networking code with '-march=native' on certain systems:
 	# https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/72026
-- 
2.43.0

